export const ABOUT_CONTENT = "# TurboDESiM Aero\n\n### Parametric Aircraft Design & Engineering Platform\n\n**Version 1.0.0**\n\nTurboDESiM Aero is a browser-based parametric aircraft design and engineering platform developed to simplify the early-stage conceptualization, configuration, analysis, and documentation of aircraft.\n\nThe platform combines **parametric aircraft geometry, 3D visualization, aerodynamic estimation, structural assessment, weight calculations, and CAD-ready geometry generation** into a unified engineering workspace — allowing engineers to move rapidly from concept to configuration without switching between disconnected tools.\n\n---\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n### ✈️ Parametric Aircraft Configuration\nBuild aircraft using dedicated components for fuselage and cross-section definition, wing geometry and placement, horizontal/vertical tail assemblies, engine nacelles and propulsion configuration, and multiple aircraft configuration templates. Changes to primary design parameters propagate through the aircraft model for rapid design-space exploration.\n\n### 📐 3D Aircraft Visualization\nInteractive WebGL-based viewport with solid, wireframe, X-ray, and exploded visualization modes, plus isometric, orthographic, top, front, side, and perspective views — no separate CAD viewer required.\n\n### 🌬️ Aerodynamic Analysis\nRapid preliminary aerodynamic evaluation covering lift coefficient, drag coefficient, lift-to-drag ratio, angle-of-attack response, lift distribution, and induced/profile drag contributions — fast feedback before committing to higher-fidelity CFD or wind-tunnel testing.\n\n### 🏗️ Structural Assessment\nPreliminary structural calculations for lifting components: wing bending assessment, distributed aerodynamic loading, shear-force and bending-moment calculation, deflection estimation, and load visualization. Intended for conceptual and preliminary design, not certification-level substantiation.\n\n### ⚖️ Weight & Balance\nPreliminary estimation of component, structural, and propulsion weight, payload/useful load, and centre-of-gravity location — helping designers understand how configuration changes affect overall mass properties.\n\n### 📦 CAD & Geometry Export\nPrepare finished configurations for downstream engineering by exporting CAD-ready geometry suitable for conventional CAD environments.\n\n---\n\n## Design Philosophy\n\n> **Make aircraft design faster, more parametric, and more accessible.**\n\nTraditional aircraft conceptual design requires several specialized tools for geometry generation, aerodynamic estimation, structural calculation, visualization, and documentation. TurboDESiM Aero brings these into a single browser-based environment:\n\n**Concept → Configuration → Geometry → Analysis → Optimization → CAD**\n\n---\n\n## Data & Design Storage\n\nTurboDESiM Aero supports **local design storage** as well as **optional cloud synchronization**. Design files can be stored locally and synchronized through connected cloud storage services. Where cloud sync is enabled, design data can be protected using client-side encryption before it ever leaves your device.\n\n**Privacy by design:**\n- AES-256-GCM encryption\n- Client-side encryption\n- Passphrase-based protection\n- Your passphrase is never uploaded\n\nYour aircraft design remains under your control.\n\n---\n\n## Who Is TurboDESiM Aero For?\n\nAerospace engineers · Aircraft designers · UAV developers · Research engineers · Engineering students · Aircraft configuration teams · Conceptual design researchers · Aerospace startups · Educational institutions\n\nParticularly useful when multiple aircraft configurations need to be created, modified, and compared rapidly.\n\n---\n\n## Engineering Disclaimer\n\nTurboDESiM Aero is intended primarily for **conceptual and preliminary engineering analysis**. Results should be independently verified before being used for detailed design, manufacturing, flight certification, safety-critical decisions, or regulatory compliance. Higher-fidelity CFD, detailed finite-element analysis, experimental validation, and certified engineering methods should be used where required. See the full Engineering & Liability Disclaimer.\n\n---\n\n**Developed by DESiM Innovations (OPC) Private Limited**\nLicensed under the Apache License 2.0.\n";

